Z||000000||billfredmike24||11-24-1999||12:55 PM||||Does anyone have Chiltons Repair Manual for the fiero and does it have instructions for replacing 85 gt clutch?  Is it good enough for anyone whos never done it before?||||reg||5
Z||000001||BENGAL4||11-24-1999||01:02 PM||||Get a Haynes manual. It is much more informative and it will take you step by step through the procedure. You can get it at Auto Zone, Pep Boys or at most major auto parts places. It cost around $11.00 US.<p>[This message has been edited by BENGAL4 (edited 11-24-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||billfredmike24||11-24-1999||01:42 PM||||Thanks Bengal4<BR>Fierostore told me to get Chiltons over Haynes, any other suggestions.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||11-24-1999||02:33 PM||||I don't think Chiltons are available any more  but one suggestion <BR>1. Buy the Haynes<BR>and <BR>2.Go to your local library and photo copy the instructions from the Chiltons||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rodrv6||11-24-1999||03:41 PM||||I have to agree with Bengal4.  The Haynes book is much more informative than the Chilton.  In some ways I think it is even better than the factory book since the Haynes books seem to be written more for the home mechanic who does not have the selection of special tools called out in the factory books.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||11-24-1999||04:41 PM||||I've always been wondering what books I have (since I never had the cover of these books). On the frontcover it simply says: "Fiero workshop manual". Are those the factory books?||||reg||5
Z||000006||Rodrv6||11-24-1999||07:48 PM||||Cliff, I have 2 factory books, one for 1984 and one for 1988.  Both of them say "Fiero Service Manual" on the front cover.  If the copyright inside is by General Motors, then they are the factory books.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Gokart||11-24-1999||09:30 PM||||I have both the Chiltons and Haynes and the Haynes is much better. More detailed instructions and PICTURES!||||reg||14
Z||000008||fierosound||11-25-1999||02:02 AM||||Helms has a website where you can find and order Factory Manuals for just about anything!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.helminc.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.helminc.com/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||geyser||11-25-1999||02:44 AM||||Get both! What one lacks the other usually has. Neither of them are as good as getting out there and getting your hands dirty. Also, the info on this forum completes most questions that are not answered in the books.||||reg||1
Z||000010||RossT||11-25-1999||04:04 AM||||The chilton was re-writtin, back in 1997. The newer version is much better than the old. The haynes is much easier to get around and find things, but the (new) chiltons has<BR>many more pictures and diagrams. Buy both! You can get the haynes from e-bay for around<BR>7 bucks.  The new chiltons I got from amazon.com for about $17. <P>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000011||ggarsk||11-25-1999||09:19 AM||||I got both the Haynes and the Clilton plus a factory service manual. With the info I get from the forum I got all bases covered.||||reg||1
